{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And behold, a ladder set up on the earth, with its top reaching to heaven, and behold, the angels of Elohim ascending and descending on it.</b> He showed him in a prophetic dream that everything done on earth is done through the agency of angels, and all is by the decree of the Most High upon them, for the angels of Elohim whom HaShem has sent to walk about on the earth do nothing, small or great, until they return to stand before the Master of all the earth and say before Him: We have walked about the earth, and behold, it sits in tranquility, or it is full of sword and blood — and He commands them to go back down to the earth and to do His word. And He showed him that He, blessed be He, stands upon the ladder, and He promises Jacob with a great promise, to make known that he will not be in the hand of angels, but will be the portion of HaShem, and He will be with him always, as He said: \"And behold, I am with you and will guard you in all wherever you go\" (Genesis 28:15), for his degree is greater than that of the rest of the righteous, about whom it is stated (Psalms 91:11): \"For His angels He will command concerning you, to guard you in all your ways.\" And according to the opinion of Rabbi Eliezer the Great (Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer 35), this vision was like the matter of the Covenant Between the Pieces to Abram, for He showed him the dominion of the four kingdoms and their ascent and their descent, and this is the reason for \"angels of Elohim,\" as it is stated regarding Daniel (Daniel 10:20, 13): \"the prince of the kingdom of Greece,\" \"and the prince of the kingdom of Persia,\" and He promised him that He, exalted be He, will be with him in all wherever he goes among them, and will guard him and deliver him from their hand. They said there in Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer: The Holy One, blessed be He, showed him four kingdoms — their dominion and their loss. He showed him the prince of the kingdom of Babylon ascending seventy rungs and descending; and He showed him the prince of the kingdom of Media ascending fifty-two rungs and descending; and He showed him the prince of the kingdom of Greece ascending a hundred and eighty rungs and descending; and He showed him the prince of the kingdom of Edom ascending and not descending. Jacob said to him: \"Yet you shall be brought down to Sheol\" (Isaiah 14:15). The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: \"If you raise yourself like the eagle...\" (Obadiah 1:4)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "Ramban quotes extensively from Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer (ch. 35); the attribution abbreviation פדר\"א and פרקי דר\"א is resolved as that work. The direct speech between Jacob and the Holy One is rendered hyper-literally as it appears, preserving the abrupt transitions."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:36:15.992204004Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}